#: ../../../whatsnew/3.16.rst:78
msgid ""
":meth:`memoryview.cast` now allows casting a multidimensional F-contiguous "
"view to a one-dimensional view. (Contributed by Jaemin Park in :gh:`91484`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../whatsnew/3.16.rst:82
msgid ""
":meth:`memoryview.cast` now accepts an *order* parameter.  With "
"``order='F'`` it returns a zero-copy Fortran-contiguous (column-major) view "
"of a flat buffer, which is useful for interfacing with column-major "
"libraries. (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in :gh:`78959`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../whatsnew/3.16.rst:88
msgid ""
":ref:`Frame objects <frame-objects>` now support :mod:`weak references "
"<weakref>`.  This allows associating extra data with active frames, for "
"example in debuggers, without keeping the frames (and everything they "
"reference) alive indefinitely. (Contributed by Łukasz Langa in :gh:`102960`.)"
msgstr ""

